WEBVTT
NOTE SYNTHETIC DEMO FIXTURE generated by scripts/make_demo_video.py

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:06.829
Welcome. Today we talk about fatigue, one of the most common complaints in Hashimoto's disease and Sjögren's disease.

00:00:07.229 --> 00:00:09.340
This is a short demonstration lecture.

00:00:09.740 --> 00:00:12.865
Thyroid hormones control how your body uses energy.

00:00:13.265 --> 00:00:19.964
The brain sends T S H, thyroid stimulating hormone, to the thyroid, which makes T4 and T3.

00:00:20.364 --> 00:00:29.614
In Hashimoto's, the immune system damages the thyroid, so it may not make enough hormone. That is hypothyroidism, and fatigue is a common symptom.

00:00:30.014 --> 00:00:31.699
Fatigue can have many causes.

00:00:32.099 --> 00:00:41.163
Even when thyroid levels are treated, tiredness may continue, because sleep problems, Sjögren's disease, low iron, or mood can all play a part.

00:00:41.563 --> 00:00:44.032
Ask your doctor which tests make sense for you.

00:00:44.432 --> 00:00:48.698
Many doctors advise taking levothyroxine on an empty stomach in the morning.

00:00:49.098 --> 00:00:55.783
Then wait thirty to sixty minutes before breakfast or coffee, because some foods and drinks can reduce how well it is absorbed.

00:00:56.183 --> 00:00:57.351
Now my own opinion.

00:00:57.751 --> 00:01:01.644
Many of my patients say they feel more energetic after cutting out gluten.

00:01:02.044 --> 00:01:05.802
I believe a gluten-free diet can reverse Hashimoto's for many people.

00:01:06.202 --> 00:01:08.413
Bring your questions to your next appointment.

00:01:08.813 --> 00:01:09.952
Thank you for watching.
